# ---- .NET build output ----
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# ---- Game data ----
# game-data/ is its OWN git repo (submodule), tracked separately from this logic-only server repo: the CSVs,
# the Lua, maps/ and SObj.tbl. Read-only at runtime; a deploy replaces it wholesale.

# ---- Live instance state — NEVER committed, to EITHER repo ----
# The counterpart to game-data/. Created by running the server, unique to this machine, and the entire
# backup target (the nightly sqlite3 .backup lives in Project1998-infra, scripts/p1998-backup.sh):
#   state/   project1998.db + its WAL sidecars, the legacy chars/*.json store, gm/tester_accounts.txt
#   logs/    server.log / login.log and their rotations. Regenerable; 80 MB of them here right now.
#   run/     restart_at / reload_now — deploy-to-server triggers, consumed and deleted on read.
#
# These are top-level SIBLINGS of game-data/ rather than living inside it, and that is what makes this
# section three lines. When state sat in the same directory as content, the content repo needed its own
# .gitignore listing every runtime filename, the deploy rsync needed the matching exclude list, and both
# had to be updated in lockstep every time something new started being written. A directory the content
# repo cannot see needs no rules at all.
state/
logs/
run/

*.log
server_live.err
server-err.log

# ---- RE tooling byproducts ----
re/__pycache__/
re/probe_log.txt
re/probe_log_533.txt
re/nametag_log.txt
scratch_*.html

# ---- client exe backups made by re/patch_*.py before an on-disk binary patch (never commit a full game exe) ----
re/*.exe
re/*.exe.bak
re/*.prenametagpatch.bak
re/patches/backups/
re/patches/**/__pycache__/

# ---- RE-tool byproducts extracted from the client PAK (regenerable via re/pak_extract.py) ----
re/monster.epf
re/monster.tbl
re/monster.pal
re/monster0.pal
re/item.tbl
re/Item.epf
re/Item.pal
re/Item.tbl
re/items_*.png
re/snd/
re/sound_log.txt
re/monsfrm.tbl
re/str_eng.res
re/nexustk_dat_list.txt
re/interdat_list.txt
# Compiled/converted client maps (game data; e.g. from re/map2cmp.py):
re/*.cmp
# Extracted from the RTK reference server / Nexus Atlas (regenerable via the tools in re/; output now lands
# in data/rtk-data/, covered by the blanket data/ rule above):
re/monster-matcher/atlas_img/
re/monster-matcher/atlas_ref.json
re/monster-matcher/cdx_monsternpc.json
re/monster-matcher/*.png

# ---- Third-party client shim (8 MB of prebuilt binaries; re-downloadable) ----
re/cnc-ddraw/

# ---- Reference server source (unkmc/RTK-Server, ~190MB; cloned for protocol reference only) ----
RTK-Server/

# runtime redirect dir written by the client
client-5.33-redirect/

re/monster-matcher/server.log

# ---- Spell-FX RE workspace (re/fx/): 19MB of PAK extracts (Effect.epf/tbl/pal/frm), scraped nexusatlas
# GIFs/HTML and the montage sheets built from them. All regenerable via re/pak_extract.py + the atlas
# scrapers. The three derived CSVs below ARE the findings, so they stay tracked.
re/fx/*
!re/fx/animation_map.csv
!re/fx/spell_animation_join.csv
!re/fx/triage.csv

# ---- Bulk sprite extracts pulled out of the client PAK for one-off inspection ----
re/out_*.epf

# ---- Timestamped snapshots the re/auto harness writes before each run ----
re/auto/*.bak
re/auto/*.bak.*
re/auto/*.csv.*.bak
